issue.body:
1) Open up in Google Chrome: http://acko.net/files/dump/paintersort/paintersort.html
2) Notice the subtle flickering on edges on the right hand side 

A few spheres are placed in the scene and their renderDepth is set manually. Some spheres are invisible on creation.

I've hacked three.js to log the webglObject.z values from the renderList array, for the first 30 frames. The invisible objects have never been rendered, hence their .z values are undefined:

``` javascript
undefined, undefined, 1, -2, 0, -1, 1, undefined, -2, 0, -1, -1, undefined, 1 
undefined, 1, undefined, undefined, 1, 1, 0, 0, -1, -1, -1, -2, -2, undefined 
undefined, undefined, undefined, undefined, 1, 1, 0, 1, -1, -1, -1, -2, -2, 0 
undefined, 1, undefined, undefined, undefined, 1, 1, 0, 0, -1, -1, -1, -2, -2 
undefined, 1, 1, 1, undefined, 0, undefined, undefined, 0, -1, -1, -1, -2, -2 
undefined, 1, 1, 1, 0, 0, -1, -1, -1, -2, undefined, -2, undefined, undefined 
undefined, undefined, 1, 1, 0, 0, -1, 1, -1, -2, undefined, -2, undefined, -1 
```

The sorting is completely unstable, and some items are misplaced (e.g. line 3 and line 7), which causes the flickering.

Logger:

``` javascript
if ( this.sortObjects ) {

  renderList.sort( painterSortStable );

  window.stfu = (window.stfu || 0) + 1;
  if (window.stfu < 30) {
    var out = [];
    for (i in renderList) (function (o) {
      if (o.z === undefined) out.push('undefined');
      else out.push(o.z);
    })(renderList[i]);
    console.log(out.join(',  '));
  }

}
```

The simplest solution seems to be to make sure webglObject.z is never undefined by initializing z to 0 on creation.

